Introduction
============

This checkout is a trimmed MicroBooNE ubana development tree prepared
to build the searchingforstrangeness package with minimal local source
overhead.

It is not the full historical ubana analysis collection.  Most legacy
ubana packages have been removed from the working tree, and the local
build now enters only the searchingforstrangeness package.


Directory layout
================

The important top-level entries are:

  CMakeLists.txt
       Top-level cetmodules build configuration.

  Modules/
       Local CMake helper modules required by the build.

  test/
       Small test harness for installed FHiCL files.

  ups/
       UPS product metadata.

  ubana/
       Package subtree entered by the top-level build.

  ubana/searchingforstrangeness
       Git submodule pointing to the searchingforstrangeness repository.


Obtaining the submodule
=======================

After cloning ubana, initialize the searchingforstrangeness submodule:

     git submodule update --init --recursive

If the submodule has already been initialized and you want the latest
recorded contents from the superproject:

     git submodule update --init --recursive --remote


Prerequisites
=============

You need the usual MicroBooNE MRB/LArSoft development environment,
including:

  * access to the MicroBooNE software container;
  * access to CVMFS and the standard MicroBooNE products;
  * an MRB development area;
  * the usual command-line tools such as mrb and lar.

This repository does not provide those dependencies itself.


Building
========

From an MRB development area, check out this repository under
srcs/ubana, initialize the submodule, and build in the normal ubana
environment.

Typical workflow:

     cd srcs/ubana
     git submodule update --init --recursive
     cd $MRB_TOP
     mrbsetenv
     mrb i -j4

The top-level build is configured to compile only:

     ubana/searchingforstrangeness

so local build time should be much lower than in a full ubana checkout.


Further information
===================

Package-specific installation and runtime notes live in the
searchingforstrangeness submodule:

  * ubana/searchingforstrangeness/INSTALL
  * ubana/searchingforstrangeness/README
  * ubana/searchingforstrangeness/USAGE


Reporting problems
==================

If the build fails, first verify:

  * the submodule is initialized;
  * the required MicroBooNE products are set up;
  * the checkout is being built inside the expected MRB/LArSoft
    environment.

If the problem is specific to the analysis package, inspect the
searchingforstrangeness repository history and configuration first,
since that package now contains nearly all analysis-specific code in
this tree.
